    chapter: "8. The 90-Day Program",
    title: "Phase 2, Days 4-14: Tour Pure rhythm foundation",
    text: "Phase 2 — Days 4–14: Tour Pure Rhythm Foundation Learn the TOUR PURE rhythm in hand, then take it to the ball. See Chapter 1 for The Rhythm, the Club Map, and Where to Lay Tour Pure.\nDAYS 4–5: Rhythm Only\n• In hand, no ball.\n• 5 sets of 10 swings saying “TOUR… PURE,” holding every finish for a count of three.\nDAYS 6–7: Letter Checkpoints\n• Slow swings, pausing at each letter: 3 sets of 10.\n• Then full rhythm with no pauses: 3 sets of 10.\n• Check 9 o'clock on every rep: the handle points up and the butt end points down at the target line.\nDAYS 8–9: Transfer to Balls — Wedges and Short Irons\n• 3 Tour Pure swings, then 1 ball, using the same words every time.\n• 30 balls with a wedge, then 20 with an 8 or 9 iron.\n• At the top of the backswing, your club's letter sits behind your trail shoulder, no higher than your ear: R in PURE for a pitching or gap wedge, E for a sand or lob wedge, U in PURE for a short iron.\nDAYS 10–11: Ground Setup — Mid and Long Irons\n• Set Tour Pure on the ground along your toe line.\n• Low Point Drill, irons (Chapter 5). Pass 8 of 10 before hitting balls.\n• Then 40 balls with a 7 iron (P) and a 5 iron or hybrid (R in TOUR). The divot starts at or just ahead of the Center Checkpoint.\nDAYS 12–13: Ground Setup — Woods and Driver\n• Same Tour Pure setup.\n• Low Point Drill, driver (Chapter 5). Pass 8 of 10 before hitting balls.\n• Then 20 balls with a fairway wood (O) and 30 with the driver (T).\n• On driver, the clubhead travels up through the ball. Sweep it off the tee rather than hitting down.\nDAY 14: Review\n• 10 balls each with a wedge, a 7 iron, and the driver, using the full rhythm.\n• Record a video of one Tour Pure swing and one club swing, and check each letter against The Rhythm in Chapter 1.",
