    text: "Phase 5 — Weeks 10–11: Scoring & Swing Refinement A short putting refresh, then scoring inside 100 yards, then woods and irons in their own blocks. You are now building a complete game, not learning from scratch.\nDAY 68: Putting Refresh — Ladder\n• Distance ladder, 5–50 ft, scored as Tap-Ins from 10 ft and beyond (out of 54). Compare your score to Day 1.\n• Then run 6 Balls around the hole.\nDAY 69: Putting Refresh — Lag and Break Points\n• Lag block from 10, 20, 30, 40, and 50 ft, 6 balls each (30 putts), scored as Tap-Ins.\n• Break point block: 10 balls on a putt breaking left, 10 on a putt breaking right.\n• Repeat the Day 3 baseline test and compare.\nNo green today? Do the home putting drills in Chapter 2: Roll It to the Center Checkpoint and Face Check.\nDAY 70: Wedge Scoring — Know Your Numbers\n• Distances at 30, 50, 70, 90, and 100 yards using the clock system and your Pitching & Chipping Distance Guide.\n• 6 balls to each distance (30 balls). Write down which wedge and swing size carries each number.\nDAY 71: Wedge Scoring — Ladder Game\n• Targets at 30, 50, 70, 90, and 100 yards.\n• 3 balls to each target going up, then 3 each coming back down (30 balls).\n• Score 1 point for every ball that finishes within 20 feet of the target. Record your score.\nDAY 72: Wedge Scoring — Random Distance Game\n• Call a yardage between 30 and 100, then hit one ball — the same as on the course.\n• 20 balls, a new yardage every ball, full pre-shot routine.\n• Score it the same way as Day 71. This is your wedge baseline.\nDAY 73: Woods Only — Fairway Woods\n• 3-wood and 5-wood off the turf (40 balls). Ball slightly forward of center. Sweep it, don't hit down.\n• Driver (20 balls). Tee height: half the ball above the crown.\n• Pre-shot routine on every ball. No irons or wedges.\nDAY 74: Woods Only — Driver\n• Driver (50 balls). Ball off the lead heel, club bottoms out at the Center Checkpoint, catch it on the way up.\n• Fairway woods (20 balls).\n• Pre-shot routine on every ball. No irons or wedges.\nDAY 75: Irons Only — Short and Mid Irons\n• 9 and 8 iron (30 balls), then 7 and 6 iron (30 balls).\n• Ball-first contact. The divot starts at or just ahead of the Center Checkpoint.\n• Hit the same ball flight 3 times in a row before changing clubs. No woods or wedges.\nDAY 76: Irons Only — Mid and Long Irons\n• 7 and 6 iron (20 balls), then 5 iron, 4 iron, or hybrid (40 balls).\n• Ball-first contact and a consistent ball flight.\n• Hit the same ball flight 3 times in a row before changing clubs. No woods or wedges.\nDAY 77: Mid-Iron Development\n• Range session (50 balls)\n• Wedge warm-up (15 balls)\n• 8 or 7 iron practice (35 balls) — path and plane focus\n• Additional practice swings with your own clubs (100 swings) — ensure full range of motion in all directions, open area free of obstacles\nDAY 78: Long Iron Practice\n• Range session (75 balls)\n• Wedge warm-up (15 balls)\n• 8–7 iron practice (30 balls)\n• 5 iron or hybrid (30 balls)\n• Additional practice swings with your own clubs (75 swings) — ensure full range of motion in all directions, open area free of obstacles",
